From 3fb1c81c62522ed70c5d02b4617987233f991be9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:47:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dock: Docked icons behave as on Window Maker: Drag, ghost,
 kaboom, menu, balloons.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Dock (`wlmdock`), the Clip's launchers (`wlmdock --clip`) and the
dock-apps now behave like Window Maker's docked icons. The compositor
handles them for `wlmdock`, from its surfaces' positions and the state.

* Dock-apps can be attached to the Dock as well as to the Clip: A dock of
  the compositor, over the Dock's column, right after its launchers. Their
  order there is stored as "Dock" in Dockapps.plist (the Clip's stays
  "Order"); started again, a dock-app returns to its dock. The number of
  them is stored as `DockappTiles` in the state's `Dock` section, for
  others placing tiles after them (eg. a system tray).
* Dragging a launcher, or a dock-app (by its border or with the move
  modifier), moves it along with the pointer, as wHandleAppIconMove. The
  ghost (see dock_fx) shows the slot it attaches to: On its own dock until
  3 tiles away from it, on the other one when right over it
  (wDockSnapIcon). Launchers go to the launchers of the Dock or the Clip,
  dock-apps to the dock-apps of either. Dropped, the icon slides into its
  slot. The Dock's main tile still drags the whole Dock.
* Dropped off the docks, a launcher is removed with Window Maker's kaboom;
  a running application's launcher stays, unless the move modifier is held
  (then without kaboom), and a locked one ("Lock = Yes") always stays. A
  dock-app explodes and is terminated: There are no free icons to leave it
  at. It is added to "Removed" in Dockapps.plist, for the session not to
  start it again; started again, it is taken off that list.
* The right button opens Window Maker's menu of the dock: "Dock position"
  (Normal, Auto raise & lower, Keep on Top) and "Add a drawer" (disabled:
  no drawers yet) for the Dock, "Clip Options" (Keep on Top, Autoraise) for
  the Clip; then "Launch", "Bring Here" (or "Unhide Here"), "Hide" (or
  "Unhide"), "Settings..." and "Kill", disabled where they don't apply. The
  Clip's launchers also have "Remove Icon"; the Dock's main tile moving
  the Dock and restoring its launchers. For dock-apps, "Settings..." holds
  their preferences, with their own actions before it. Launchers'
  "Settings..." runs `DockSettingsCommand` of the configuration, as
  `<command> launcher Dock|Clip <index>`. "Bring Here", "Hide" and "Kill"
  act on the windows with the launcher's `AppID`.
* The Dock's and the Clip's level, stored as Window Maker's `Lowered` and
  `AutoRaiseLower`: Below the windows (Normal), above (Keep on Top, the
  default), or raised after 600 ms on the dock and lowered 1 s after
  leaving it. Also for the surfaces of `wlmdock`.
* Balloons, as Window Maker's for docked icons: The name (AppID, or the
  program) and the command, for launchers and dock-apps; the workspace's
  name on the Clip, when longer than 5 characters.
* pt_BR: Window Maker's translations for the menu ("Executar", "Trazer
  aqui", "Esconder", "Configurações...", "Terminar", ...).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
